  "query_preview": "..\nA surface trough extending between Invest 96W to the east-southeast \nand Tropical Depression 28W to the north-northwest will encroach upon\nSaipan and Tinian tonight and linger through Thursday, bringing\nscattered showers and isolated thunderstorms. The zones were split \ndue to short-term differences in shower coverage as drier air will \nremain over Guam and Rota. Island-effect showers may be possible for\nthese islands, but easterly winds are expected to advect these \nshowers over western coastal waters, similar to the pattern that \noccurred today. Afterwards, isolated showers will return for the \nentire region through Friday night. Then, weather conditions may \nbegin to deteriorate Saturday as Invest 96W potentially tracks \nthrough the Marianas as a tropical storm or typhoon. Widespread \nlocally heavy showers, near-gale winds, and thunderstorms are \nforecast from Saturday night through Sunday night, with a peak of the\nworst conditions around Sunday. Shortly afterwards, shower coverage \nlooks to decrease to isolated with light and variable winds possibly \nreturning after Monday night. Residents of the Marianas should \ncontinue storm preparations and stay up to date with the forecasts in\nthe coming days.",
